{
  "id": "situated-cognition",
  "term": "situated cognition",
  "definition": "Situated cognition is the view that thinking does not occur in isolation but depends on a person’s bodily form, ongoing interaction with the environment, use of physical supports, and social-cultural context. In this view, cognitive activity is embodied, enacted, extended, and embedded rather than being only an abstract process located in the brain or body.",
